  "known_boundaries": [
    "SQLite remains single-instance; PostgreSQL is required for multi-control-plane shared state",
    "Redis is optional and not authoritative for queue or metadata",
    "distributed non-paid AI queue has at-least-once retry semantics after worker lease expiry",
    "paid jobs are not automatically replayed after expired worker lease",
    "all replicas must share the same CF_DISTRIBUTED_DATA_KEY; key rotation is manual",
    "no PostgreSQL HA failover, multi-region consensus or Kubernetes operator is bundled",
    "no real PostgreSQL/Redis integration run unless CF_TEST_POSTGRES_URL is provided",
    "no production load benchmark or independent security certification",
    "Live PostgreSQL integration tests include shared workflow claim/reclaim but are skipped unless CF_TEST_POSTGRES_URL points to a disposable database",
    "Private-network binding is opt-in and requires an explicit trusted reverse-proxy CIDR allowlist; public and unspecified binds are rejected",
    "Security source products must be installed/configured separately and emit supported JSON/JSONL formats",
    "Six source adapters normalize selected metadata; they are not full product-specific SIEM/EDR API connectors",
    "Playbooks are data-only: no endpoint isolation, process termination, firewall changes, arbitrary command execution or remote shell",
    "No real Wazuh, Suricata, Zeek, Falco, Trivy or osquery production service was connected in the build environment",
    "Three PostgreSQL live integration tests are skipped unless CF_TEST_POSTGRES_URL points to a disposable PostgreSQL database",
    "Continuous tailer supports append-oriented JSONL from Wazuh, Suricata, Zeek, Falco and osquery; Trivy remains batch-based",
    "Telemetry shipping is at-least-once; acknowledged batches can replay after a crash before checkpoint commit and rely on stable source event IDs for server deduplication",
    "copytruncate detection is best-effort if truncation and rapid regrowth occur between polls; rename rotation recovery requires the rotated inode to remain available",
    "MITRE ATT&CK labels and cross-source correlation scores are heuristic candidates, not proof or attribution",
    "AI Analyst submits sanitized normalized evidence through the configured AI queue; upstream provider retention/privacy terms still apply",
    "No real Wazuh, Suricata, Zeek, Falco, Trivy or osquery production source was connected during build verification",
    "Continuous tailer systemd template is installed but never enabled automatically; source log permissions must be granted explicitly",
    "Security correlation and ATT&CK mapping are bounded heuristic candidates, not probability estimates or attribution",
    "Zeek flat dotted JSON fields are supported; source-specific field semantics still depend on upstream version/configuration",
    "Continuous tailer live integration was tested against a local CyberForge loopback API and SQLite, not against production Wazuh/Suricata/Zeek/Falco/osquery services",
    "No AI response actions, endpoint isolation, process termination, firewall change or remote command execution is performed by the Security Analyst",
    "Systemd telemetry unit was syntax-verified but not installed/enabled on a separate customer Linux host"
  ],
